OpenArena 0.8.8 base-game data for Pyxis
Upstream: https://openarena.ws/
Archive: https://download.tuxfamily.org/openarena/rel/088/openarena-0.8.8.zip
SHA-256: 5a8faf7f5b51f351b0a1618c06b6b98a5f1a6758f1d39818de2c87df2a0bac4a

This recipe copies the nine baseoa PK3 archives unchanged. It includes the
upstream COPYING, CREDITS, README and both release readmes. Additional credits
and licences remain inside the PK3s. No foreign operating system engine,
library, executable or missionpack is staged separately.

The assets are copyrighted by the OpenArena Team, id Software and the many
individual contributors named in the included credits and per-asset notices.
Debian's corresponding split-package copyright reviews classify most assets
as GPL version 2 or later. The merman model in pak2-players and the oa_thor map
in pak6-patch088 carry GPL version 2 only notices. The included pul1duel map
notice also specifies GPLv2. Preserve these notices and use GPL version 2 for
the aggregate; this recipe does not grant later-version rights to those files.
COPYING contains the GNU General Public License version 2.

The PK3s contain compiled QVM game modules as well as exported models, maps,
textures, music, sounds and recorded demos. Calling this a data package does
not remove corresponding-source obligations. Their corresponding sources are
supplied as separate public downloads next to the binary package, not installed
game files. See SOURCES.txt and
source-downloads.sha256 for the location, exact filenames and SHA-256 pins.
The eight Debian asset source snapshots preserve the supplied editable forms
and exported payloads; separate matching-version game C sources cover the
retained QVMs. Manual asset export and bit-reproducible QVM builds are not
claimed. Original copyright, README, build rules and Debian source records
accompany the downloads.

